  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>3f315e17ae2222d83b68195367672623</srcmd5>
    <version>1.5.5</version>
    <time>1786543938</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 1.5.5

Upstream raises its langchain-core floor from &gt;= 1.5.2 to &gt;= 1.5.4; that is
the only dependency change. The floor is encoded honestly rather than
lowered, which makes this a lockstep pair with python-langchain-core 1.5.4,
submitted alongside it -- please take the two together.

The ordering is a convenience rather than a landmine: 1.5.5 was also built
and tested against langchain-core 1.5.3 and passed all 194 tests, because
OutputTokenDetails, the one new import, already exists there. So the floor
reflects upstream's declared minimum, not a hard runtime requirement.

Verified on aarch64 against langchain-core 1.5.4: 194 tests passed on each of
python313 and python314, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings.</comment>
    <requestid>1370781</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="7" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>83a5d0088da2a6699c55c75d2cfded3a</srcmd5>
    <version>1.5.6</version>
    <time>1786738013</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-langchain-anthropic to 1.5.6

- Normalize tool_search_tool_result blocks so that streaming-only index
  fields are no longer sent back to the Anthropic API
- Correct model profile data for Claude Fable 5, Sonnet 5 and Opus 4.1

Dependency floors are unchanged from 1.5.5 (langchain-core &gt;= 1.5.4,
anthropic &gt;= 0.120.0, pydantic &gt;= 2.7.4).

Built and tested natively on aarch64: 195 tests pass per Python flavour
(python313, python314), rpmlint clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1371027</requestid>
  </revision>
